{
  "description": "A map of sets of number tuples, one holding an unknown, converts to a map of lists of string tuples",
  "spec": [
    "spec.md#collection-and-structural-type-conversions",
    "spec.md#unknown-values-and-the-dynamic-pseudo-type",
    "ext/typeexpr/README.md#the-convert-cty-function"
  ],
  "op": "eval",
  "features": [
    "typed-values",
    "unknown-values",
    "functions",
    "type-expressions"
  ],
  "notes": "The set holding an unknown element may have one element or two, so it converts to an unknown list. hashicorp/hcl first converts it to an unknown list of the set's own element type, tuple([number]) (conversionCollectionToList in go-cty's cty/convert/conversion_collection.go), and then unifies the map's converted elements with safe conversions only (conversionUnifyCollectionElements), which turn it into an unknown list of tuple([string]).",
  "variables": {
